---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="About DailyRadar - Curated Daily Directory of New Tools"
  description="Learn about DailyRadar, our automated curation methodology, and our mission to highlight indie software and open source projects."
  canonicalUrl="https://radar.yourdomain.com/about"
>
  <div style="max-width: 750px; margin: 2rem auto; line-height: 1.8;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 2.25rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--card-border); padding-bottom: 0.75rem;">
      About DailyRadar
    </h1>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--accent);">
        Our Mission
      </h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Every single day, thousands of passionate independent creators, open source contributors, and innovative engineering teams launch incredible software tools across GitHub, Hacker News, and Product Hunt.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
        However, the internet is loud, and genuine breakthrough tools often get drowned out by massive ad-funded incumbent software. <strong>DailyRadar</strong> was built to solve this problem: an automated, noise-free directory providing daily curation of brand-new developer utilities, AI apps, and open-source alternatives.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--accent);">
        How It Works
      </h2>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
        <li><strong>Continuous Monitoring:</strong> Our automated crawlers scan GitHub Trending, Hacker News Show, and Product Hunt every 24 hours.</li>
        <li><strong>Quality Filtering:</strong> We filter out low-effort spam, broken links, and duplicate marketing buzz to surface practical, usable software.</li>
        <li><strong>Structured Organization:</strong> Each tool is cataloged by functional category, pricing tier, open-source status, and alternatives.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--accent);">
        Contact & Feedback
      </h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
        Have a question, feedback, or a tool you'd like to see featured? Feel free to reach out via GitHub or email. We are constantly improving our parsing and categorization engines.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
